{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Have you since your days</b> — since the day you were created, you commanded to bring forth the morning and made known to the dawn its place." "<b>And can you grasp the wings of the earth</b> — the correct interpretation is that it speaks of the dawn, that it grasps the wings of the earth and the wicked die every day and perish, as in: 'The sinners shall cease from the earth' (Psalm 104:35). Even though the righteous man dies, the kindness of YHWH is upon those who fear Him, and His righteousness upon children's children."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:01.825020608Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}